  "bossParagraphs": {
    "easy": [
      [
        "the naga rises from the flooded baray",
        "hold the terrace until the venom runs dry"
      ],
      [
        "moss and root have taken the outer wall",
        "speak the old words and drive it back"
      ],
      [
        "lanterns gutter along the broken colonnade",
        "name the guardian and the temple will stand"
      ],
      [
        "seven stone heads turn toward the causeway",
        "meet them here and do not step back"
      ],
      [
        "the moat is black and the bridge is long",
        "type every name the water gives you"
      ],
      [
        "apsara watch from the gallery above",
        "give them a reason to keep watching"
      ]
    ],
    "medium": [
      [
        "krong reap walks the causeway of the dead",
        "the laterite splits beneath every step he takes",
        "answer him now or the sanctuary is lost"
      ],
      [
        "the monsoon breaks over the ruined gopura",
        "his shadow drowns the frieze of churning seas",
        "hold the last terrace and do not falter"
      ],
      [
        "a thousand faces watch from the crumbling spire",
        "the demon king comes for the reliquary within",
        "unmake him with the names carved in the stone"
      ],
      [
        "smoke of the censer bends away from his tread",
        "garuda and naga alike have fled the gallery",
        "you are what is left standing on the stair"
      ],
      [
        "the bells in the north tower have gone silent",
        "something older than the temple is awake",
        "keep the words coming and it cannot land"
      ],
      [
        "he crosses the moat without troubling the water",
        "every lamp in the outer gallery leans away",
        "hold the line of the doorway and speak"
      ],
      [
        "the causeway lions turn their heads to follow",
        "dust lifts from the flagstones and hangs there",
        "name each shadow before it reaches the step"
      ],
      [
        "the library roof gave way in the first hour",
        "palm leaf and ash are all that is left of it",
        "say what was written there and mean it"
      ],
      [
        "he asks for the temple by its oldest name",
        "do not give it to him and do not stop typing",
        "the stone remembers who defended it"
      ],
      [
        "rain runs upward along the carved pilasters",
        "the guardian figures have closed their eyes",
        "open them again with the words you know"
      ],
      [
        "his crown is made of the seven fallen towers",
        "each one still has a name that can be spoken",
        "speak them in order and take the crown apart"
      ],
      [
        "the plaza has filled with things that were buried",
        "they came up when he called and they answer to him",
        "cut the thread between them and hold the gate"
      ]
    ],
    "hard": [
      [
        "the sarcophagus in the innermost sanctum stands open",
        "every lintel of the temple bleeds verdigris and ash",
        "there is no ward left here but the words you carry"
      ],
      [
        "an unseasonal darkness swallows the afternoon entirely",
        "the moat boils and the causeway cracks lengthwise",
        "finish the invocation before the temple forgets itself"
      ],
      [
        "he speaks and the inscriptions peel from the gopura",
        "the consecrated brazier gutters out in the antechamber",
        "recite the deconsecration and unmake his procession"
      ],
      [
        "krong reap wears the crown of the seven terraces",
        "his retinue of revenants encircles the sanctuary wall",
        "articulate every syllable or the ward will not hold"
      ],
      [
        "the apsara have turned their faces to the wall",
        "an unremembered language runs beneath the flagstones",
        "transliterate it faster than he can rewrite the stone"
      ],
      [
        "the reliquary has been prised from its pedestal",
        "reliquary dust hangs incandescent in the still air",
        "reconstitute the litany before the last mote settles"
      ],
      [
        "his shadow precedes him by the length of the causeway",
        "the balustrade serpents have abandoned their posts",
        "enunciate the guardian names in unbroken succession"
      ],
      [
        "the bas relief of the churning sea has begun to move",
        "asuras and devas alike have let go of the serpent",
        "restore the equilibrium with nothing but your hands"
      ],
      [
        "an interminable procession climbs the eastern stair",
        "each figure carries a fragment of the broken lintel",
        "assemble the inscription before they reach the summit"
      ],
      [
        "the sanctuary vault exhales centuries of trapped air",
        "every carved apsara is weeping a granular black dust",
        "consecrate the threshold again and refuse him entry"
      ],
      [
        "he pronounces the temple deconsecrated and abandoned",
        "the pediment sculptures crumble to acknowledge him",
        "contradict him with the whole architecture of the word"
      ],
      [
        "the last unbroken naga balustrade fractures audibly",
        "his crown is an accumulation of everything he has taken",
        "disassemble it syllable by deliberate syllable"
      ]
    ],
    "endless": [
      [
        "the serpent is older than the stone it guards",
        "it has swallowed every name ever carved here",
        "it will swallow yours and keep on going"
      ],
      [
        "there is no last terrace and no last tower",
        "the jungle takes back everything it is given",
        "type until the temple stops asking you to"
      ],
      [
        "the causeway runs further than it did yesterday",
        "nothing you clear stays cleared for very long",
        "keep going anyway because that is the whole point"
      ],
      [
        "another shape resolves out of the treeline",
        "there is no count and there is no ending",
        "hold the doorway for as long as you are able"
      ]
    ]
  },
